            <ArticleTitle>A double-blind evaluation of the effect of amlodipine on ambulatory blood pressure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S24-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effects of amlodipine on ambulatory blood pressure were investigated in patients with mild-to-moderate hypertension. Ambulatory recordings showed that amlodipine maintained diastolic and systolic blood pressure below baseline levels for a full 24-h period without altering the normal circadian rhythm. No reflex tachycardia occurred and side effects were rare.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
